## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design an end-to-end, edge-friendly CV pipeline under realistic wearable constraints. It tests understanding of how to balance 2D detection with 3D pose estimation from monocular input, proficiency in on-device few-shot adaptation, temporal stability, and data strategies that bridge synthetic and real domains.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight hybrid detection and pose estimation models
- 6-DoF pose estimation from monocular imagery
- On-device few-shot adaptation with object exemplars
- Temporal consistency and edge latency trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
class ARObjectEstimator {
  constructor(config) {
    this.detector = new LightweightDetector(config.detector);
    this.poseHead = new PoseHead(config.pose);
    this.temporalModule = new TemporalConsistency();
    this.prototypeMemory = new PrototypeMemory(config.memory);
  }

  estimate(frame, adaptations = []) {
    const detections = this.detector.detect(frame);
    const poses = detections.map(d => {
      const initialPose = this.poseHead.predict(d.bbox, d.features);
      return this.temporalModule.refine(initialPose, d.keypoints);
    });
    return this.prototypeMemory.adapt(poses, adaptations);
  }
}
```

